description:
Within my javascript project I am attempting to use the latest tree-sitter-r.wasm with the tree-sitter.wasm from the web-tree-sitter npm package. However, upon attempting to load the language:

```
        const parser = new TreeSitter.Parser();
        const R = await TreeSitter.Language.load('/tree-sitter-r.wasm');
        parser.setLanguage(R);
```

I get an error about versions: `Incompatible language version 0. Compatibility range 13 through 15.`

```r
fn(
  NULL = ,
)

fn(
  NA = ,
)

fn(
  Inf = ,
)

fn2(
  a = ,
)
```

The first 3 fail to parse, but the last succeeds

But this succeeds

```r
fn(
  NULL = 1,
)
```

I _think_ we need to allow newlines right here

https://github.com/r-lib/tree-sitter-r/blob/c8b6e5f3f3c055cfc76471ebc912286e9e73d7d2/grammar.js#L241-L242

Newlines _before_ the `else` are handled specially by the external scanner, but this is valid R code and is marked as an ERROR right now:

```r
# can do this for some reason
if (1) {
  "hi"
} else
{
  "ugh"
}


# cant do this - handled by external scanner
if (1) {
  "hi"
} 
else {
  "ugh"
}
```
